-- REFINEMENT ------- errors/refinement_violated_19.march

refinement violation: index must not be negative [refinement_violated]
argument `n` of `List.nth` does not satisfy precondition `_ >= 0`
for example, when `i` is `-1`
note: guard the call (e.g. `if i >= 0 && i < List.length(items) do List.nth(items, i) else … end`) or pass a value known to satisfy it

7 |     if i < 0 do List.nth(items, i) else 0 end
                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `List.nth_opt` is `List.nth` without the requirement: it returns `Option` instead of panicking.
        match List.nth_opt(items, i) do
          Some(v) -> …
          None -> …
        end

    this argument must satisfy `i >= 0`:

7 |     if i < 0 do List.nth(items, i) else 0 end
                                    ^

    `i` comes from here:

6 |   fn at(items : List(Int), i : Int) : Int do
                               ^

    the call is reached only when this is true:

7 |     if i < 0 do List.nth(items, i) else 0 end
           ^^^^^
    run `march --explain refinement_violated`


